  "query_preview": ".. (Sunday through Next Thursday)\nAn upper-level shortwave trough traversing the Canadian \nPrairies will track a weak surface low well to our north on \nSunday. Model guidance remains in good agreement keeping any \nprecipitation well north of the local forecast area, generally \nalong and north of the Illinois/Wisconsin state line. Warm air \nadvection ahead of this system will bring a brief uptick in \ntemperatures on Sunday, boosting afternoon highs into the mid- \nto-upper 70s.\n\nIn the wake of the low, another expansive surface high \noverspreads the Midwest by early Monday before settling along \nthe Mid-Atlantic coast by midweek. Highs Monday and Tuesday will\nremain near to slightly below normal in the upper 60s and lower\n70s with lows consistently in the 40s. By Wednesday and \nThursday, return southwesterly flow around the backside of the \ndeparting ridge will initiate a more sustained warming trend \nacross the region. Afternoon highs are expected to reach the \nupper 70s to low 80s through the latter half of next week with \npersistent dry conditions expected.",
